学|to study; to learn|学习|xuéxí|to study|我每天学习中文。|Wǒ měitiān xuéxí Zhōngwén.|I study Chinese every day.|A child (子) under a roof wearing a glowing cap of knowledge, learning to read.
儿|child; son|儿子|érzi|son|他的儿子五岁了。|Tā de érzi wǔ suì le.|His son is five years old.|Two little legs walking forward, picturing a young child taking steps.
子|child; seed; noun suffix|孩子|háizi|child|这个孩子很聪明。|Zhège háizi hěn cōngmíng.|This child is very smart.|A baby wrapped in a swaddle with both arms outstretched for a hug.
天|sky; day; heaven|今天|jīntiān|today|今天天气很好。|Jīntiān tiānqì hěn hǎo.|The weather is very nice today.|A person (大) standing with the vast sky stretching as a horizontal line above their head.
上|up; above; to go up|上午|shàngwǔ|morning|我上午去学校。|Wǒ shàngwǔ qù xuéxiào.|I go to school in the morning.|A vertical pointer standing clearly above the baseline, pointing upward.
下|down; below; to go down|下午|xiàwǔ|afternoon|我们下午见。|Wǒmen xiàwǔ jiàn.|See you in the afternoon.|A vertical line hanging down below the ground line, pointing downward.
不|not; no|不是|bú shì|is not; no|这不是我的书。|Zhè bú shì wǒ de shū.|This is not my book.|A bird flying straight up toward the sky line, refusing to come down.
好|good; fine; well|你好|nǐ hǎo|hello|你好，很高兴认识你。|Nǐ hǎo, hěn gāoxìng rènshi nǐ.|Hello, nice to meet you.|A mother (女) holding her child (子) safely in her arms represents everything good.
有|to have; there is|没有|méiyǒu|do not have|我有一本中文书。|Wǒ yǒu yì běn Zhōngwén shū.|I have a Chinese book.|A hand reaching out at the top to hold a piece of meat (月) underneath.
那|that; then|那里|nàlǐ|there|那是谁的杯子？|Nà shì shuí de bēizi?|Whose cup is that?|Pointing past the village wall (阝) toward something far over there.
午|noon; midday|中午|zhōngwǔ|noon|我们中午一起吃饭。|Wǒmen zhōngwǔ yìqǐ chīfàn.|We eat lunch together at noon.|The sun reaches the highest crossbeam at midday, marking noon.
们|plural marker for people|我们|wǒmen|we; us|我们是好朋友。|Wǒmen shì hǎo péngyou.|We are good friends.|A person (亻) walking through a doorway (门) to join a group of people.
小|small; little|小姐|xiǎojiě|Miss; young lady|这只小猫很可爱。|Zhè zhī xiǎomāo hěn kě'ài.|This little cat is very cute.|A vertical line dividing two tiny dust specks on either side.
一|one; single|一个|yí gè|one (item)|我有一个苹果。|Wǒ yǒu yí gè píngguǒ.|I have one apple.|A single horizontal stroke drawn cleanly across the page.
这|this; here|这里|zhèlǐ|here|这是我的老师。|Zhè shì wǒ de lǎoshī.|This is my teacher.|Walking (辶) right up to the literature (文) directly in front of you right here.
么|interrogative or suffix particle|什么|shénme|what|你想吃什么？|Nǐ xiǎng chī shénme?|What would you like to eat?|A light trailing thread that hooks onto words to form questions like "what".
大|big; large; great|大学|dàxué|university|这个房间很大。|Zhège fángjiān hěn dà.|This room is very big.|A person standing tall with both arms and legs stretched out wide.
个|general measure word|个人|gèrén|individual; personal|家里有三个人。|Jiālǐ yǒu sān gè rén.|There are three people in the family.|A bamboo roof pointing up above a single vertical stalk standing alone.
字|character; word; letter|汉字|Hànzì|Chinese character|这个字怎么读？|Zhège zì zěnme dú?|How do you read this character?|A child (子) sitting under a school roof (宀) practicing written characters.
年|year|今年|jīnnián|this year|今年我二十岁。|Jīnnián wǒ èrshí suì.|I am twenty years old this year.|Stacked grain stalks harvested once every four seasons to mark a full year.
在|at; in; on; to exist|现在|xiànzài|now|他在家看书。|Tā zài jiā kànshū.|He is reading at home.|Planting firm roots into the earth (土) to stay present right where you are.
多|many; much; more|多少|duōshǎo|how many; how much|这里有很多人。|Zhèlǐ yǒu hěn duō rén.|There are many people here.|Two evenings (夕) stacked together mean many nights have passed.
少|few; little; less|不少|bùshǎo|quite a few|今天人很少。|Jīntiān rén hěn shǎo.|There are very few people today.|Start with something small (小) and slice a stroke off the bottom to leave even less.
家|home; family; house|家人|jiārén|family members|我晚上八点回家。|Wǒ wǎnshang bā diǎn huíjiā.|I go home at eight in the evening.|A sturdy roof (宀) sheltering a domesticated pig (豕), the traditional symbol of a settled family home.
书|book; letter; to write|看书|kànshū|to read a book|我喜欢看历史书。|Wǒ xǐhuan kàn lìshǐ shū.|I like reading history books.|Layered bamboo slips bound together with a brush stroke running down the spine.
你|you (singular)|你们|nǐmen|you (plural)|你叫什么名字？|Nǐ jiào shénme míngzi?|What is your name?|A person (亻) standing beside a small target (尔) as you point and speak to them.
时|time; hour; season|时间|shíjiān|time|现在是什么时候？|Xiànzài shì shénme shíhou?|What time is it now?|Measuring the movement of the sun (日) inch by inch (寸) to track time.
我|I; me|我们|wǒmen|we; us|我是中国人。|Wǒ shì Zhōngguórén.|I am Chinese.|A hand holding a ceremonial halberd (戈) upright to stand up for oneself.
的|possessive or descriptive particle|我的|wǒ de|my; mine|这是我的电脑。|Zhè shì wǒ de diànnǎo.|This is my computer.|A bright white (白) target hit squarely by a spoon-shaped mark (勺) showing clear ownership.
对|correct; right; toward|对不起|duìbuqǐ|sorry; excuse me|你说得很对。|Nǐ shuō de hěn duì.|What you said is very right.|Two hands working in precise measure (寸) until everything matches up right.
分|minute; to divide; part|分钟|fēnzhōng|minute|请等我五分钟。|Qǐng děng wǒ wǔ fēnzhōng.|Please wait five minutes for me.|A sharp knife (刀) cleanly splitting something in two (八) equal parts.
汉|Han Chinese; Chinese language|汉语|Hànyǔ|Chinese language|他的汉语说得很好。|Tā de Hànyǔ shuō de hěn hǎo.|He speaks Chinese very well.|Flowing water (氵) of the Han River paired with a steady hand (又) of culture.
今|now; today; present|今天|jīntiān|today|今天是星期一。|Jīntiān shì Xīngqīyī.|Today is Monday.|A roof-like cover gathering the present moment right underneath it.
国|country; nation; state|中国|Zhōngguó|China|你去过哪个国家？|Nǐ qùguo nǎge guójiā?|Which countries have you visited?|A precious jade treasure (玉) protected inside four strong border walls (囗).
去|to go; to leave|去年|qùnián|last year|我明天去北京。|Wǒ míngtiān qù Běijīng.|I am going to Beijing tomorrow.|Stepping off the ground (土) and striding forward to leave for a new place.
人|person; people; human|人们|rénmen|people|他是一个很好的人。|Tā shì yí gè hěn hǎo de rén.|He is a very good person.|Two legs striding steadily across the ground like a walking person.
他|he; him|他们|tāmen|they; them|他是我的同学。|Tā shì wǒ de tóngxué.|He is my classmate.|A person (亻) standing beside the phonetic component 也 to refer to him.
她|she; her|她们|tāmen|they (female)|她是一位医生。|Tā shì yí wèi yīshēng.|She is a doctor.|The female radical (女) paired with 也 to specifically mean she and her.
爱|to love; to like|爱好|àihào|hobby; interest|我爱我的家人。|Wǒ ài wǒ de jiārén.|I love my family.|Gentle fingers (爫) sheltering a warm friend (友) under one roof.
八|eight|八月|bāyuè|August|他八点去上班。|Tā bā diǎn qù shàngbān.|He goes to work at eight o'clock.|Two strokes parting cleanly to the left and right, open and balanced like eight.
爸|father; dad|爸爸|bàba|dad; father|我爸爸在做饭。|Wǒ bàba zài zuòfàn.|My dad is cooking.|The father radical (父) on top of 巴, the warm everyday word for dad.
打|to hit; to play; to make (a call)|打电话|dǎ diànhuà|to make a phone call|我给你打电话。|Wǒ gěi nǐ dǎ diànhuà.|I will give you a phone call.|A hand (扌) striking a nail (丁) squarely on the head.
二|two|二十|èrshí|twenty|我有两本书，他在二楼。|Wǒ yǒu liǎng běn shū, tā zài èr lóu.|I have two books, and he is on the second floor.|Two parallel horizontal lines stacked neatly one above the other.
作|to do; work; to write|工作|gōngzuò|job; to work|你的工作忙吗？|Nǐ de gōngzuò máng ma?|Is your job busy?|A person (亻) rising up early (乍) to start the day's work.
工|work; labor; skill|工人|gōngrén|worker|他今天不工作。|Tā jīntiān bù gōngzuò.|He is not working today.|A carpenter's square connecting heaven and earth through skilled craft.
后|back; behind; after|后面|hòumiàn|behind; at the back|学校在医院后面。|Xuéxiào zài yīyuàn hòumiàn.|The school is behind the hospital.|Trailing under a cliff canopy with a mouth (口) calling from behind.
会|can; be able to; meeting|开会|kāihuì|to have a meeting|我会说一点儿中文。|Wǒ huì shuō yìdiǎnr Zhōngwén.|I can speak a little Chinese.|People gathering under a wide roof (人) above rising clouds (云) for a meeting.
叫|to call; to be called|名字叫|míngzi jiào|to be named|请问你叫什么？|Qǐngwèn nǐ jiào shénme?|May I ask what your name is?|An open mouth (口) calling out loudly so the voice carries far.
九|nine|九月|jiǔyuè|September|现在是早上九点。|Xiànzài shì zǎoshang jiǔ diǎn.|It is nine o'clock in the morning now.|An arm bending and reaching out with all its strength just before ten.
来|to come; to arrive|回来|huílái|to come back|欢迎你来中国。|Huānyíng nǐ lái Zhōngguó.|Welcome to China.|Heavy ears of wheat ripening on a stalk, bringing the harvest home.
了|completed action or change particle|太好了|tài hǎo le|great; wonderful|我已经吃过饭了。|Wǒ yǐjīng chīguò fàn le.|I have already eaten.|A quick, clean hook stroke showing that an action is wrapped up and done.
六|six|星期六|Xīngqīliù|Saturday|我们六点下班。|Wǒmen liù diǎn xiàbān.|We get off work at six o'clock.|A roof lid (亠) resting over two little legs (八) standing wide apart.
妈|mother; mom|妈妈|māma|mom; mother|我妈妈是老师。|Wǒ māma shì lǎoshī.|My mom is a teacher.|A woman (女) with the phonetic horse (马) component, the universal sound for mom.
吗|question particle for yes/no|好吗|hǎo ma|okay?; is it good?|你是学生吗？|Nǐ shì xuésheng ma?|Are you a student?|A mouth (口) adding the 马 sound at the end of a sentence to ask a question.
